WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.770
The Walking Dead saw some drastic changes
during its ninth season, raising countless

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.080
questions about season 10.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.520
With the season premiere arriving soon, we've
gone ahead and pulled together everything

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.299
you need to know heading into the tenth year
of dramatic, complex, gruesome zombie madness.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:19.000
For those wondering what The Walking Dead
has in store for its tenth season, an extensive

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.100
trailer was released at Comic-Con in July
2019.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.279
One of the primary themes of the trailer was
fear — not of the undead, but rather of

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.760
the very much alive Alpha and her army of
Whisperers, both of which featured prominently

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:31.920
throughout season 9.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.800
The animalistic villains appear to be a central
part of the new season and could lead to an

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.820
all-out war at some point down the road.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.200
Before we dive into any new additions to the
cast, it's worth taking a quick trip down

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:46.149
memory lane to remember the primary characters
that the show lost in the catastrophically

00:00:46.149 --> 00:00:47.860
violent course of season 9.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.379
Rick Grimes may not be dead, but he disappeared
early on, after he successfully blew up the

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:55.199
bridge to stop a horde of zombies from gaining
access.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.020
On top of that, there was the mysterious disappearance
of Maggie Rhee.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.720
Adding to the list, we also have Jesus, who
was killed off in the fading moments of the

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.800
mid-season finale.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.070
And finally, there's season 9's penultimate
episode, which ended with ten heads on pikes

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.520
on Alpha's creepy new border wall, including
Tara, Henry, Tammy, and Enid's.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.760
Season 9 of The Walking Dead was highlighted
by the departure of major cast members like

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.620
Andrew Lincoln and Lauren Cohan, and it turned
out that was just the beginning.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:23.260
Months before season 10's premiere, it was
already a well-established fact that Danai

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.990
Gurira, who plays the fearless Michonne, would
be leaving the show at some point during the

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.040
upcoming season.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.470
At this point, reports seem to indicate that
Michonne will be present throughout most of

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.580
the season, which should give viewers plenty
of time to prepare for her exit.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:39.020
There are only two main characters, not counting
Rick, who have made it from the dark days

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.480
of season 1 all the way to the decade mark:
Daryl and Carol.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:46.640
Season 9 had a massive six-year time jump
that drastically changed the status quo for

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:47.560
both characters.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.640
Post time-jump, Daryl was seen living off
on his own, while "Queen Carol" had married

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.140
King Ezekiel and adopted Henry as her son.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.840
By the end of the season, Daryl is drawn out
of seclusion and back into the unraveling

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.140
events with the Whisperers and Carol loses
Henry, breaks up with Ezekiel, and abdicates

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:02.700
her crown.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:07.140
The season 10 trailer seems to promise even
more changes for the long-time fan favorite

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:07.640
characters.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.819
Season 9 had plenty of different plotlines
to follow, but one that stood out from the

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.849
bunch was the interesting parallel between
Carol and Alpha.

00:02:14.849 --> 00:02:18.189
The two mothers have been to hell and back
again ever since the apocalypse hit.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:22.010
Both are powerful, indomitable characters,
but they've developed dramatically different

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.140
philosophies about post-apocalyptic life.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.040
This was already interesting to watch as their
children met and became infatuated with each

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:28.540
other.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.260
On the one hand, Alpha watched as her daughter
was converted from the Whisperer ways and

00:02:32.269 --> 00:02:34.219
ultimately taken under Carol's wing.

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:38.109
On the other hand, Carol faced trauma yet
again when her adopted son Henry was abducted

00:02:38.109 --> 00:02:41.220
by Alpha and then decapitated for her gruesome
border wall.

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:45.760
All of these similarities and grievances set
the pair up for an epic showdown, and it appears

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.900
that season 10 is where that clash of wills
is going to take place.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.160
Actress Melissa McBride has already declared
that she thinks there should be a confrontation,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.980
telling the Hall H audience at San Diego Comic-Con
that:

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.269
"I feel like there deserves to be one, Carol
wants vengeance."

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.400
On top of that, showrunner Angela Kang has
also expressed excitement for the two women

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.879
to clash, adding that:

00:03:04.879 --> 00:03:08.379
"...They’re both two incredibly powerful
women, who just happen to be on opposite sides

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.980
of this kind of epic struggle that is happening
between our people and the Whisperers.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.320
So there’s just some really cool stuff up
ahead."

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:19.200
Season 10 looks to promise plenty of problems
for the heroes of The Walking Dead.

00:03:19.209 --> 00:03:23.950
In fact, there are not one, not two, but three
primary villains already in the cards.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:24.920
First off, there's Negan.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:28.500
Season 9 revealed a character that was both
humbled and even a bit heroic.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:32.709
Season 10 promises to continue the conflicted
character's storyline, with showrunner Kang

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:34.820
confirming that he'll be released from prison.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.360
On The Talking Dead, she said:

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.460
"Negan is a guy that likes to be in the middle
of things, and being in a jail cell means

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:42.319
he's definitely not in the middle of things."

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.480
Negan drama aside, the show also has to deal
with the new baddie on the block: Alpha.

00:03:46.629 --> 00:03:49.980
The horrifyingly calm leader of the Whisperers
showed her villainous chops throughout the

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:50.800
previous year.

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:04.880
On top of Alpha and her musclebound sidekick,
Beta, the new season is also set to debut

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.360
Gamma, a Whisperer who is ultra loyal to Alpha
and her agenda

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.140
Along with a host of other changes, season
9 showed that weather can play a serious role

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.580
in The Walking Dead storyline.

00:04:14.849 --> 00:04:18.840
The season finale revealed a picturesque winter
landscape, dotted with rotting bodies and

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:23.040
shuffling corpses, all of which provided some
chilling new territory for the serial thriller.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.580
The change in scenery was a fun twist to the
show's typically hot, southern setting.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.200
And the good news is, it's not the last we'll
see of environmental challenges.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:43.020
Showrunner Angela Kang told Entertainment
Weekly that:

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:46.890
"We're still exploring other kinds of environmental
obstacles that we haven't done and seen before,

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.060
so there will be some other new stuff to look
out for."

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:53.371
The promotional material has already hinted
at a couple of new natural phenomena, with

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.820
one scene showing what appears to be some
characters in front of a forest fire.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.080
Oceanside and its waterfront location also
seem likely to factor into the new season,

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:05.160
opening up the doors to some aquatic adventures
— something that The Walking Dead's sister

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.380
show Fear the Walking Dead already explored
in its second season.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.800
The massive six-year leap in season 9 had
far-reaching repercussions.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.400
It introduced the mysterious issue of Michonne
and Daryl's scars, aged Judith Grimes into

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:21.340
a force to be reckoned with, surprised everyone
with her little brother, and saw a growing

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.640
divide among the communities.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:26.260
With all of the shifting around, one would
think the show would settle down to a regularly

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:30.690
paced timeline at some point, but that's not
happening yet, and AMC isn't even trying to

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:32.000
make it a surprise this time.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.540
Season 9 ended with a jump forward into the
winter.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:38.910
Now, season 10 is poised to start with yet
another jump months ahead into the following

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:39.400
spring.

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.240
While the constant shifts are a bit jarring,
it does accelerate the age of the younger

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:44.240
generation.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.500
This could serve as a perfect catalyst to
eventually tie in with the second spin-off

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.270
series, which will be set far in the future
and will follow the lives of the first generation

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.880
of humans to grow up in the post-apocalyptic
world.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:59.310
As you probably recall, season 9 saw Rick
Grimes removed from the flagship Walking Dead

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.580
series, but not killed off.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:05.210
Instead, the intrepid hero found himself washed
downstream along with a host of walkers, only

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.800
to be picked up by a mysterious helicopter
and flown off.

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:11.800
Since then, the question of what happened
to Rick has come up over and over again.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.290
Michonne was still struggling with the loss
six years later, and Daryl seemed ready to

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.160
head off into the sunset looking for his friend
at any moment.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:22.520
The hints are likely to continue coming in
season 10, as the world gears up for the planned

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.200
Rick Grimes trio of films.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:28.180
This is especially likely since the hero's
storyline has even been spilling over into

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:31.900
the spin-off series Fear the Walking Dead,
where what looked to be the same helicopter

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.290
was spotted in one episode.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.600
Whatever the time and place, it's certain
that the Rick Grimes saga will continue at

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.100
some point.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:42.040
Whether it ever crosses back into the flagship
series or not, though, that isn't stopping

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:46.140
the hint-happy production team from penciling
in more clues about the hero's whereabouts.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:50.020
While the situation remains steeped in mystery,
there is one meeting we can hope to see once

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:50.520
again.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.040
We're talking about a reunion between Rick
and Daryl.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:57.700
The two brothers in arms shared a very emotional
last few episodes together, spent tussling,

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.380
trapped in a pit, and finally making up.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.120
"Brother, take my hand."

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:11.690
The connection between the two characters
is tried and true, and the possibility of

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:15.180
their finally finding their way back to one
another again is certainly in the cards at

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:15.680
this point.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:20.020
In an interview at San Diego Comic-Con, former
The Walking Dead showrunner Scott Gimple was

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:22.150
asked if Daryl would ever see Rick again.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:23.350
He responded by saying:

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:24.570
"…I can't rule that out.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:27.200
Have you seen a little film When Harry Met
Sally?

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.470
That's how they're going to rejoin again."

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:33.860
In related news, there's also the juicy potential
for season 10 to feature the return of absentee

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:35.140
hilltop commander Maggie.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:39.640
Actress Lauren Cohan's brief excursion to
her own show on ABC looks like it may end

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.540
with a quick round trip right back into the
arms of the undead.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.180
While the failure of Cohan's new show to get
off the ground isn't necessarily enough of

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.330
a reason to assume that the fan-favorite actress
will return, there's reason to hope.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:54.090
Angela Kang went right ahead and poured fuel
on the fire by making it clear that they're

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:56.440
doing their best to make her return a reality.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:57.680
She told EW that:

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.260
"I’m not sure if I can say much about it
right now actually.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.180
I’ll just say that we’re working on it.”

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.930
Clearly, they haven't given up on re-integrating
Maggie back into the story.

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.480
Like Rick, she was never killed off.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.400
In fact, she was referenced multiple times
throughout season 9 and appeared to be off

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.890
on other business in an undisclosed location.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:18.150
If that's not enough, promotional material
for season 10 seems to be hinting to a return

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.150
appearance.

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:22.600
One sneak peek shown on The Talking Dead directly
references "letters from Maggie."

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.080
"Find what you were looking for?"

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:30.040
"Oh, sailed down southward Oceanside's been
picking up letters from Maggie?

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.460
Wasn't anything there."

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.180
Whatever the show has in store for Cohan's
character, it hardly seems like she's going

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.860
to shuffle off this mortal coil anytime soon.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:42.479
Another factor to keep in mind going into
the tenth season is the soon-to-be lack of

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:44.280
source material for the show to follow.

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.960
There's no doubt that the onscreen version
of The Walking Dead has already charted a

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.180
course all its own.

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:52.850
The comics have always served as a grounding
point from which the show could draw inspiration,

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:54.149
characters, and storylines.

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:58.040
But the truth is, the showrunners have never
shied away from altering things as they go

00:08:58.040 --> 00:08:58.540
along.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.200
Carl's death, Michonne and Rick's relationship,
Shane's extended lifespan, the very existence

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:07.310
of Daryl were all cinematic alterations that
don't have their origins in print.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:11.280
That said, one question worth asking is how
things would look if there was no source material

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:11.780
at all.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:14.240
The answer may be forthcoming sooner than
expected.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:18.519
Just months before the season 10 release date,
The Walking Dead co-creator Robert Kirkman

00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:22.620
shocked fans with a one-two punch that no
one saw coming in the comic series.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.910
Spoilers incoming.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:27.420
First, he suddenly and unexpectedly killed
off Rick Grimes.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.740
Then, he followed it up with a final installment
and the announcement that the comic book series

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:32.980
was officially over.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:37.120
With this sudden imposition of a hard ending
to the source material, it will be interesting

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.750
to see how AMC handles their ten-year TWD
universe plans.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.960
We'll just have to see what that looks like
when the new season arrives on October 6th.

